WORKFLOW (executed in analysis.py, all parts reproducible):
1. Data reading: invaded_niche_pathways.csv (632 plots, tab-sep) as the habitat-resolved prevalence dataset; invasion_success_pathways.csv (81 species) for the species-level companion; temporal_trends_contingency_table.csv for framing; phylogenetic_tree.txt for PGLS.
2. Primary metric: per-habitat occupancy prevalence = proportion of plots with n.gard>0, with Wilson 95% CIs; secondary metrics mean n.gard (bootstrap CI) and relative dominance n.gard/n.total.
3. Unadjusted tests: chi-square (chi2=139.4, df=9, p=1.3e-25, Cramer V=0.470); logistic regression presence ~ habitat (reference Scrublands, McFadden R2=0.243) with 45 pairwise contrasts, BH-FDR correction (22 significant); Poisson count model LRT (chi2=196.1, df=9) with mild overdispersion (phi=1.14); Negative-Binomial vs Zero-Inflated-NB comparison (ZINB better, llf -333 vs -500).
4. Diagnostics: Moran's I on model residuals via inverse-distance weights (50 km) with permutation test; VIF among standardized covariates (elevation 12.9, temperature 18.5 -> collinear; others <7).
5. Adjusted model: logistic presence ~ habitat + elevation + urban/cropland 2009 (1000 m) + road/stream distance + temperature + rainfall + 1956-2009 landscape-change proxy; LRT of habitat given covariates (chi2=58.5, p=2.7e-9); marginal occupancy per habitat at observed covariate values; Spearman rho=+0.976 vs unadjusted; stability check dropping temperature.
6. Species companion: medians/means by pathway, Kruskal-Wallis and Mann-Whitney (gardening vs unintentional) on invaded plots, 10km AOO, habitat.range, invaded niche breadth, mrt; PGLS (Brownian covariance from Newick tree) for habitat.range (gardening coef -1.10, p=0.013) vs OLS comparison.
7. Temporal framing: gardening share of introductions by period (17% -> 75%).
8. Outputs: results/prevalence_by_habitat.csv, logit_pairwise_contrasts.csv, prevalence_by_habitat.svg, final_hypothesis.txt, full_analysis_log.txt.
